/// @brief Error set of all possible errors of this Core module
error ErrEnv:
	VarNotFound("Requested variable not set"),
	InvalidName("Name contains illegal characters"),
	InvalidValue("Value cannot be used (e.g. embedded NUL)");

/// @brief Returns the content of the given environment variable
///
/// @param `variable` The environment variable to get the content from
/// @return `str` The content of the environment variable
///
/// @note This function will throw an error if the environment variable couldnt be found
def get_env(str variable) -> str {ErrEnv};

/// @brief Sets the given environment variable to the given value
///
/// @param `variable` The environment variable to set
/// @param `value` The value to set the variable to
/// @param `overwrite` Whether to overwrite the variable if its already present.
/// @return `bool` Whether the value was written into the variable
///
/// @note The returned value of the function behaves like shown in this table:
///       | overwrite | already exists | return value |
///       |-----------|----------------|--------------|
///       | false     | false          | true         |
///       | false     | true           | false        |
///       | true      | false          | true         |
///       | true      | true           | true         |
def set_env(str variable, str value, bool overwrite) -> bool {ErrEnv};
